# CLAUDE.md — {{project.name}}

{{project.description}}. Code is the source of truth. This file is the index and the law;
canonical documents hold the depth.

The framework core is project-agnostic and lives in `framework/`; everything that changes
between projects lives in `project-context/`. Read `framework/README.md` once, then
`framework/rules/invariants.md`.

## 0. `{{kb.root}}framework/**` is READ-ONLY (FI-25)

**Do not create, edit, move or delete any file under the core.** This binds every agent, in
every task, including the lead. A need that does not fit is answered in this project's context,
or by an extension beside the core (FI-26), or by a task to whoever maintains the core — never
by editing it. Do not push a core change: everyone consuming the core inherits it, so publishing
one is a release.

Two rules an agent can only learn here, because this is the file every agent loads:

- **The anchor `kb.root` is `{{kb.root}}`** — this line is where an agent resolves it. A file
  outside the unit cites `{{kb.root}}framework/…`; a file inside it cites `framework/…`,
  knowledge-base-relative (FI-27).
- **Example material is read-gated and binds nothing (FI-24).** It is opened only when the task
  prompt carries the grant `EXAMPLE-ACCESS:` naming what is needed from it, and it never becomes
  precedent.

